<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1718" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀέριος</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾱ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>; 
			Ion.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠέριος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span> (q.v.): (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀήρ</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>misty</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκότον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					1534
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>in the air, high in air</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρότον ποδῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					546
				</span></i>
			; <i>of the air, aerial</i>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χθόνιος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				27
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῦρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Vict.</u>
					1.10
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰτίαι ἀ.</span>, title of work
			by <i><span class="en">
				Democr.
			</span></i>; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπόγειος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PMag.Lond.</u>
				121.893
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. φύσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Mu.</u>
					392b14
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζῷα</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				398b33
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γένος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Epin.</u>
					984e
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Prom.Es</u>
					6
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Iamb.
					<u>Myst.</u>
					1.9
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>wide as air, infinite</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄμμου μέγεθος ἀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					1.33
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				5.42
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>indefinite, vain, futile</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phld.
				<u>Vit.</u>
				p.9J.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ir.</u>
				p.79
			</span></i> W.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιζήτησις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Sign.</u>
					21
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
